{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Continuity correction on f789: new typed bridge library functions and MCP tools are additive; rebar.reconcile(mode=...), MCP reconcile(mode=...), and bridge_fsck remain callable with their published defaults/schemas. Updated ACs require real old/new parity, unified 0/1/2 core disposition, retained schema negotiation, and mcp.allow_jira_sync coverage for both new and compatibility mutating routes. Expanded structured file impact across public exports, models, server registration, types, schemas, tests, and docs."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786215027057034001,"uuid":"03b03179-a84a-4025-918c-d2669580552b"}